", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d92345b9"}, {"id": "fa0b6e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>615</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d92345ba"}, {"id": "55c787", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d92345bb"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:35.507Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:35.507Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d92346b1"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d92346a9", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234688", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205a2"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475f"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4715"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> travels in a medium with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and a photon of radiation of linear momentum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> travels in a vacuum. The wavelength of the photon is ____ times the wavelength of the particle."}, "options": [{"id": "f9e69e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234689"}, {"id": "953afa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923468a"}, {"id": "5247ce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923468b"}, {"id": "0c730b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923468c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923468d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205a2"], "topics": ["60d2d1d1185d7a32fa320586"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4706"], "question": {"text": "When light of frequency twice the threshold frequency is incident on the metal plate, the maximum velocity of emitted electron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When the frequency of incident radiation is increased to five times the threshold value, the maximum velocity of emitted electron becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "8498f3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923468e"}, {"id": "7f1f86", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923468f"}, {"id": "08c177", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234690"}, {"id": "4ec775", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234691"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234692", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205a2"], "topics": ["60d2d1d1185d7a32fa320586"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c6843"], "question": {"text": "When radiation of wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;is used to illuminate a metallic surface, the stopping potential is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. When the same surface is illuminated with radiation of wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, the stopping potential is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. If the threshold wavelength for the metallic surface is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;then value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "e9b7c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234693"}, {"id": "2d2608", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234694"}, {"id": "6b39dc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234695"}, {"id": "b283bb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234696"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234697", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205a2"], "topics": ["60d2d1d1185d7a32fa320586"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f02"], "question": {"text": "A point source of light is placed at the centre of curvature of a hemispherical surface. The source emits a power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>.&nbsp;The radius of curvature of hemisphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and the inner surface is completely reflecting. The force on the hemisphere due to the light falling on it is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "3c5ecb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234698"}, {"id": "0193d4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9234699"}, {"id": "7f31b8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923469a"}, {"id": "650313", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923469b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923469c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205a2"], "topics": ["60d2d1d1185d7a32fa320586"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b7"], "question": {"text": "The surface of a metal is illuminated alternately with photons of energies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively.&nbsp;The ratio of maximum speeds of the photoelectrons emitted in the two cases is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The work function of the metal in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is..........<br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "d0d2c4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923469d"}, {"id": "003b6a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923469e"}, {"id": "fd3cf6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d923469f"}, {"id": "78b1aa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d92346a0"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45